---
import BaseLayout from "../../../shared/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { MAIN_SITE_URL } from "../../../shared/config/config";

const OPERATOR_INFO = "{OPERATOR-INFO}";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Health & Medical Disclaimer",
  url: MAIN_SITE_URL + "/disclaimer/",
  description: "This platform provides educational information about problematic pornography use. It is not medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.",
  isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "name": "Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform", "url": "https://selfcontrolatlas.com" },
};
---
<BaseLayout
  siteTitle="Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  siteUrl={MAIN_SITE_URL}
  title="Health & Medical Disclaimer"
  description="This platform provides educational information about problematic pornography use. It is not medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment."
  canonical="/disclaimer/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Disclaimer", url: "/disclaimer/" }]}
>
<h1>Health &amp; Medical Disclaimer</h1>
<p>This website provides general educational information about problematic pornography use
(PPU), compulsive sexual behavior, and related recovery experiences. By using this site,
you acknowledge and agree to the following. This disclaimer is important — please read it.</p>
<p><strong>Last updated: 2026-10-23</strong> · <strong>Last reviewed: 2026-10-23</strong></p>

<h2>1. Not medical advice</h2>
<p>Nothing on this site is medical advice, diagnosis, treatment, or a substitute for
consultation with a qualified healthcare professional. The site does not establish a
doctor–patient or therapist–client relationship, and no page on this site should be read as
a diagnosis or a treatment plan.</p>
<p>If you have a medical or mental-health concern, consult a qualified professional — a
doctor, psychiatrist, psychologist, licensed therapist, or counselor. Do not delay or
forego professional care because of anything you read here.</p>

<h2>2. Not individualized</h2>
<p>The content is general information. It does <strong>not</strong> take into account your
personal circumstances, health history, situation, or needs. What is true "on average" or
"for some people" may not be true or safe for you. General information cannot account for
co-occurring conditions, medications, or your specific context.</p>

<h2>3. Not psychological or therapeutic advice</h2>
<p>Recovery from compulsive sexual behavior can involve psychological factors. This site is
not psychotherapy, coaching, or counseling. It does not provide therapeutic guidance, and
it does not monitor your progress. If you are working with a therapist, follow their
guidance over anything you read here.</p>
<p>The site may describe techniques discussed in recovery communities (for example,
cognitive-behavioral strategies, mindfulness, or accountability practices). Describing a
technique is not the same as recommending or administering it.</p>

<h2>4. Experiences are not evidence</h2>
<p>Personal experiences and community patterns describe what some people reported. They do
<strong>not</strong> establish that a strategy, timeline, or outcome applies to you. An
experience is one person's account, not a scientific finding — and not a promise about your
situation. A pattern is a recurring observation, not a proven effect.</p>

<h2>5. Evidence is summarized, not complete</h2>
<p>Research summaries reflect the sources available at the time of writing and may be
superseded by newer studies. The site's evidence tiers (see the <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>)
indicate how much weight a given source carries, but no summary here is a comprehensive
literature review or a clinical guideline.</p>
<p>Research on problematic pornography use is evolving, and findings can be mixed or
contested. Where evidence is uncertain, the site says so — but you should still verify
important health information with a professional or a primary source.</p>

<h2>6. No guarantee of results</h2>
<p>The site does not promise that any strategy, timeline, or outcome — including the "90-day"
framing common in recovery communities — will work for you. Recovery is individual. No
outcome is guaranteed. Any improvement, setback, or timeline reported by one person is not
a prediction of yours.</p>

<h2>7. Seek professional help when needed</h2>
<p>If you experience significant distress, depression, anxiety, intrusive thoughts, or
thoughts of self-harm, contact a qualified professional or local emergency services.
Reaching out is a reasonable, common, and serious step — not a failure.</p>
<p>You do not need to wait until things are "bad enough" to seek help. Early, professional
support is often the most effective.</p>

<h2>8. If you are in crisis</h2>
<p>If you are in immediate danger or thinking about harming yourself, contact local
emergency services right now, or use a helpline listed on the <a href="/crisis-resources/">Crisis Resources</a>
page. This site is not monitored in real time and cannot provide crisis support. Do not
wait for a reply from this site.</p>

<h2>9. Adult content notice</h2>
<p>This site discusses adult topics, including pornography, compulsive sexual behavior, and
sexual health. It is intended for adults (18+). The site itself contains no adult media, but
the subject matter is mature and may not be appropriate for minors.</p>

<h2>10. No endorsement of linked resources</h2>
<p>Links to external resources (research, classifications, crisis services) are provided for
reference. A link is not an endorsement, and we do not control the content or practices of
linked sites. Mention of a product, approach, or service does not constitute a
recommendation.</p>

<h2>11. Operator and liability</h2>
<p>This site is operated by <strong>{OPERATOR_INFO}</strong>. To the maximum extent
permitted by law, the operator and its editors are not liable for decisions made based on
this site's content. Use is at your own discretion. See the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>
for the full liability statement.</p>

<h2>12. No professional relationship</h2>
<p>Using this site does not create a professional relationship of any kind — medical,
psychological, therapeutic, or legal — between you and the operator or its editors.</p>

<h2>13. Scope of this disclaimer</h2>
<p>This disclaimer applies to all content on this site, including experience records,
community patterns, problem answers, strategy pages, research summaries, and the knowledge
base. It also applies to any content you access through links from this site only to the
extent such linked content is under the operator's control; third-party sites have their own
terms and disclaimers.</p>

<h2>14. Not a diagnostic tool</h2>
<p>No questionnaire, checklist, or self-assessment on this site is a diagnostic tool. The
site does not diagnose compulsive sexual behavior disorder (CSBD) or any other condition.
If you are concerned about whether your behavior constitutes a problem, consult a qualified
professional.</p>

<h2>15. Frequently asked questions</h2>
<p><strong>Is this site written by doctors?</strong> No. Content is not authored or reviewed by named medical professionals, and we do not claim it is.</p>
<p><strong>Can I rely on this site for treatment?</strong> No. It is educational information, not treatment.</p>
<p><strong>Does the site guarantee recovery?</strong> No. No outcome is guaranteed.</p>
<p><strong>What if I'm in crisis?</strong> Contact local emergency services or a helpline on the <a href="/crisis-resources/">Crisis Resources</a> page.</p>
<p><strong>Does this site contain adult content?</strong> It discusses adult topics but contains no adult media. It is intended for adults.</p>

<h2>16. If you disagree</h2>
<p>If you do not agree with this disclaimer, do not use the site. Continuing to use the site
means you accept it.</p>

<p><em>Last updated: 2026-10-23.</em></p>
</BaseLayout>
